Android's cRSubTracks::Init (000850d4) reads Track: 0-6 as track sets 0-6 and
Track: r as 8, and its cRSubGame::StartLevel (000817ac) picks the random space
backdrop and flip, then a random fringe colour (GetSkirtColourRandom, 0006c624),
only for 8 (the `cmp r3, 8` at 00081a7c). Windows reads Track: r as 5, which
Android's Pro 1-5 use as a track set, with their own SpacePro background. The
shell parses the track sets and samples the colour (extras_skirt_colour_random).

